recovery: opt-in unattended sideload for bring-up, and a stage crash fix

On debuggable builds with debug.recovery.auto_sideload=true, a plain recovery
boot starts ADB sideload at once and (debug.recovery.auto_reboot=true) reboots
after a successful install. Skips the userdata mount when /adb_keys is already
embedded, allows a longer sideload timeout via debug.recovery.sideload_timeout,
and fixes an inverted std::optional check in start_recovery() that crashed
when no stage was set.

